---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const feedUrl = (import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PODCAST_FEED_URL || '').trim();
const nextMusicPlayer = 'https://github.com/leerob/next-music-player';
---

<Layout
	title="Podcast · Train Market Data"
	description="Podcast desk on Train: RSS hooks, episode placeholders, and links to player patterns."
	pageClass="page-podcast"
	eyebrow="Podcast"
	subtitle="Static shell for show notes, RSS, and an embedded player once you host audio off GitHub Pages."
>
	<section class="container podcast-shell">
		<header class="podcast-hero card">
			<div>
				<h1 class="podcast-title">Podcast</h1>
				<p class="muted podcast-lead">
					Train stays a <strong>static site</strong>. This tab is the home for a future <strong>audio program</strong>: show
					notes, chapter markers, and outbound links to your feed or a dedicated player app. For a full-featured listening
					UI pattern (queue, transcripts, mobile layout), see{' '}
					<a href={nextMusicPlayer} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">leerob/next-music-player</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="podcast-hero-aside">
				{
					feedUrl ? (
						<>
							<p class="mono small muted">PUBLIC_PODCAST_FEED_URL</p>
							<a class="button" href={feedUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
								Open RSS / Atom feed
							</a>
						</>
					) : (
						<p class="mono small muted">
							Set <code class="podcast-code">PUBLIC_PODCAST_FEED_URL</code> at build time to surface a button to your public
							feed.
						</p>
					)
				}
				<a class="button-secondary" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}sports/`}>
					Sports · live scoreboard
				</a>
				<a class="button-secondary" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}broadcast/`}>
					Broadcast desk
				</a>
			</div>
		</header>

		<div class="podcast-grid">
			<article class="card podcast-card">
				<h2 class="podcast-card-title">Feed &amp; metadata</h2>
				<p class="muted small">
					Publish RSS or Atom from your host; Train only links. Episode art, duration, and enclosure URLs stay in the feed —
					no server execution on Pages.
				</p>
			</article>
			<article class="card podcast-card">
				<h2 class="podcast-card-title">Embedded player</h2>
				<p class="muted small">
					When you have an HTTPS origin that allows framing, add an iframe or web component here (same pattern as the
					Broadcast desk embed guardrails).
				</p>
			</article>
			<article class="card podcast-card">
				<h2 class="podcast-card-title">Show notes</h2>
				<p class="muted small">
					Markdown or MDX routes can list seasons and episodes; wire build-time data or a headless CMS when you outgrow
					placeholders.
				</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.podcast-shell {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 20px;
		padding-top: 6px;
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.podcast-hero {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: flex-start;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 20px;
	}

	.podcast-title {
		margin: 0 0 10px;
		font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}

	.podcast-lead {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 62ch;
		line-height: 1.55;
	}

	.podcast-lead a {
		color: rgba(169, 200, 255, 0.95);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 3px;
	}

	.podcast-hero-aside {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: stretch;
		gap: 10px;
		min-width: min(100%, 240px);
	}

	.podcast-code {
		font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
		font-size: 0.92em;
		padding: 1px 6px;
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
		border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
	}

	.podcast-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
		gap: 16px;
	}

	.podcast-card-title {
		margin: 0 0 8px;
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.podcast-card p {
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}
</style>
